Fixed — without an assertion, since expects belong in test files and can't be encapsulated in
components.

  const rows = section.getByRole('button', { name: /^Remove/ });
  const rowCountBeforeAdd = await rows.count();
  await addOutboundMappingButton(heading).click();
  await rows.nth(rowCountBeforeAdd).waitFor({ state: 'visible' });

nth(rowCountBeforeAdd) is the row just added, so the .last() lookups can no longer resolve to the
previous row.

It would have failed rather than saved silently — the verification step asserts both regular_tag
and govern_tag are present — but still a flake worth removing.

